Yeah.

1229
01:04:53.500 --> 01:05:00.880
So listen, people out there, if you are ever in these situations where you're having this problem that Nate is describing,

1230
01:05:01.080 --> 01:05:01.880
go get checked out.

1231
01:05:02.000 --> 01:05:06.800
And it's not just your hearing because you can take a hearing test and pass the hearing teSt.

1232
01:05:07.380 --> 01:05:14.000
But you might still have this auditory processing disorder, which makes it hard for your brain to process what it is hearing.

1233
01:05:14.180 --> 01:05:19.800
And there's exercises you can do to improve this and make life a lot easier for yourself.

1234
01:05:20.060 --> 01:05:21.000
Throwing it out there.

1235
01:05:21.160 --> 01:05:26.740
I find this all very interesting and something I wouldn't have thought about until you started sharing it.

1236
01:05:26.940 --> 01:05:29.360
Well, I really appreciate all the mail we got from people.

1237
01:05:29.540 --> 01:05:32.660
And I always like it when people see themselves represented.

1238
01:05:33.060 --> 01:05:33.440
Yeah.

1239
01:05:33.440 --> 01:05:35.060
This is a real disorder.

1240
01:05:35.320 --> 01:05:36.940
And so I thought it would be cool to bring it up.

1241
01:05:37.660 --> 01:05:37.880
Yeah.

1242
01:05:38.340 --> 01:05:39.640
I'm so glad you did.

1243
01:05:40.120 --> 01:05:44.920
Back in the warehouse, they finally decided to go with Kevin's plan, I guess.

1244
01:05:45.080 --> 01:05:49.280
They're going to grease the floor and slide boxes to the truck.

1245
01:05:49.460 --> 01:05:54.760
There was a deleted scene where Jim says, I can't believe in all the years the warehouse was here,

1246
01:05:54.900 --> 01:06:01.680
they didn't just simply back the truck up into the warehouse and then you could just easily load it.

1247
01:06:01.680 --> 01:06:03.740
So he's like, let's do this.

1248
01:06:03.820 --> 01:06:05.080
And he has Dwight back it up.

1249
01:06:05.260 --> 01:06:08.560
But what you realize really quickly is the truck is too big.

1250
01:06:08.680 --> 01:06:10.860
The driveway is too narrow to turn in.

1251
01:06:11.120 --> 01:06:12.240
You can't make the turn.

1252
01:06:12.800 --> 01:06:16.560
Dwight clips the side of the warehouse building and gets the truck stuck.

1253
01:06:17.080 --> 01:06:21.660
And then that's what leads Jim and Dwight to be like, OK, let's try the slide method.

1254
01:06:21.840 --> 01:06:25.220
And that's why in the shots you can see now the truck is closer.

1255
01:06:25.460 --> 01:06:27.320
It's kind of wedged into the warehouse.

1256
01:06:27.320 --> 01:06:28.100
I didn't notice that.

1257
01:06:28.400 --> 01:06:28.840
Yeah.

1258
01:06:29.520 --> 01:06:33.980
Well, Steve Burgess had mentioned in his breakdown that deleted scene you just mentioned.

1259
01:06:34.340 --> 01:06:36.720
Rain really did drive the truck into the wall.

1260
01:06:37.040 --> 01:06:39.160
Rain did all his own stunts for this episode.

1261
01:06:39.680 --> 01:06:40.700
It's a big truck.

1262
01:06:40.940 --> 01:06:43.160
He was very Keanu in this episode.

1263
01:06:43.380 --> 01:06:44.540
Yes, he was.

1264
01:06:44.720 --> 01:06:48.680
Well, Angela, in this scene at around 16 minutes,

1265
01:06:49.160 --> 01:06:55.100
a bunch of boxes look like they careen into the camera operator.

1266
01:06:55.100 --> 01:06:58.300
Yeah, I clocked it at 16 minutes, 43 seconds.

1267
01:06:58.480 --> 01:07:00.060
Looks like it takes out the camera guy.

1268
01:07:00.540 --> 01:07:06.200
Well, Allie G from Topeka, Kansas, would like to know if this was scripted or just an actual accident.

1269
01:07:06.940 --> 01:07:09.640
Well, Allie, I was very curious as well.

1270
01:07:09.800 --> 01:07:10.980
I went to the shooting draft.

1271
01:07:11.140 --> 01:07:11.940
Here's what it said.

1272
01:07:12.280 --> 01:07:13.120
B-roll.

1273
01:07:13.420 --> 01:07:18.320
Jim and Dwight place a box of paper on a garbage can lid and slide it on a finished track,

1274
01:07:18.480 --> 01:07:20.580
which stops well short of the mark.

1275
01:07:20.740 --> 01:07:24.640
They slingshot a box with a rope and it goes flying out the door.

1276
01:07:24.640 --> 01:07:31.680
They slingshot another box toward a truck tire, which ricochets off and knocks over a cameraman.

1277
01:07:32.320 --> 01:07:32.540
Hey!

1278
01:07:34.700 --> 01:07:35.360
Amazing!

1279
01:07:35.820 --> 01:07:37.040
It was scripted.

1280
01:07:37.460 --> 01:07:41.800
Well, Steve Burgess said that he seems to remember that no matter what we did,

1281
01:07:41.960 --> 01:07:45.640
they could not get the boxes to really slide very well.

1282
01:07:45.900 --> 01:07:48.180
He said it was really, really hard.

1283
01:07:48.180 --> 01:07:56.900
They did use, like, a kind of silicon grease on the ground, but the friction was too much.

1284
01:07:57.040 --> 01:07:58.940
The boxes would not slide.

1285
01:07:58.940 --> 01:08:00.880
They had to cheat this so much.

1286
01:08:01.680 --> 01:08:06.500
You know, if you really watch carefully, whenever they try to slide them, they don't go very far.

1287
01:08:06.720 --> 01:08:07.260
I know.

1288
01:08:07.260 --> 01:08:09.340
Oh, I know.

1289
01:08:09.740 --> 01:08:15.020
Clearly, in the script, they imagine that these boxes could just go, like, flying all the way out the door.

1290
01:08:15.300 --> 01:08:15.480
No.

1291
01:08:15.740 --> 01:08:17.180
They were never going to travel that far.

1292
01:08:17.840 --> 01:08:22.320
Jim and Dwight are going to have a joint talking head where they say they have to move these boxes,

1293
01:08:22.320 --> 01:08:24.660
so sadly, this has become the best idea.

1294
01:08:24.960 --> 01:08:27.980
I mean, clearly, they can't believe they're following Kevin's idea.

1295
01:08:27.980 --> 01:08:33.860
But while they're talking about this, Kevin slips on grease behind them and falls down really hard.

1296
01:08:34.620 --> 01:08:34.760
Yeah.

1297
01:08:35.060 --> 01:08:42.780
Steve Burgess said that the stunt coordinators put a big old mattress back there and that Brian really did do that fall himself.

1298
01:08:43.100 --> 01:08:43.940
Good job, Brian.

1299
01:08:43.940 --> 01:08:47.880
It looks so painful, but he fell on a soft, cushy mattress.

1300
01:08:48.340 --> 01:08:54.500
Well, now we're going to find out some new information about Daryl, which is he has decided he would like to be fired.

1301
01:08:55.040 --> 01:08:55.540
Yeah.

1302
01:08:55.540 --> 01:09:01.140
And he's trying to introduce them to the new warehouse crew down there in Hank's Corner.

1303
01:09:01.420 --> 01:09:01.940
What's it called?

1304
01:09:02.080 --> 01:09:02.920
Caffeine Corner.

1305
01:09:03.180 --> 01:09:04.160
Run by Hank.

1306
01:09:04.780 --> 01:09:05.140
Yes.

1307
01:09:05.380 --> 01:09:06.320
Owned by Dwight.

1308
01:09:06.720 --> 01:09:06.880
Right.

1309
01:09:07.700 --> 01:09:09.440
Daryl's like, I don't want to meet these people.

1310
01:09:09.600 --> 01:09:10.980
In fact, I just want to be fired.

1311
01:09:11.420 --> 01:09:18.760
And Andy kind of pushes back and I guess, like, re-inspires Daryl to love his job again.

1312
01:09:19.420 --> 01:09:19.660
Yeah.

1313
01:09:19.840 --> 01:09:21.340
Well, Daryl gives him an ultimatum.

1314
01:09:21.420 --> 01:09:23.480
He says, fire me or make me the manager.

1315
01:09:23.480 --> 01:09:24.420
I earned it.

1316
01:09:24.420 --> 01:09:27.140
And Andy pushes back and says, no, this is my job.

1317
01:09:27.300 --> 01:09:28.040
I earned it.

1318
01:09:28.280 --> 01:09:30.060
You had a chance for it.

1319
01:09:30.260 --> 01:09:32.160
And there were a few things they noted.

1320
01:09:32.340 --> 01:09:33.420
I looked in your file.

1321
01:09:33.580 --> 01:09:36.920
You hired your friend to replace you who wasn't qualified.

1322
01:09:36.920 --> 01:09:38.080
They clocked that.

1323
01:09:38.260 --> 01:09:40.020
He goes on to list a few things.

1324
01:09:40.160 --> 01:09:44.060
And then he says, and what happened to, you know, business school at night?

1325
01:09:44.540 --> 01:09:46.860
And he says, well, D'Angelo died.

1326
01:09:46.920 --> 01:09:47.760
He goes, he didn't die.

1327
01:09:47.880 --> 01:09:48.660
His brain died.

1328
01:09:49.920 --> 01:09:52.420
And he said, but I'm manager now.

1329
01:09:52.640 --> 01:09:55.680
I would approve you to go to night school, but you haven't asked.

1330
01:09:55.680 --> 01:09:58.280
So, you know, what do you want here?

1331
01:09:58.800 --> 01:10:00.040
Do you want a job?

1332
01:10:00.200 --> 01:10:02.080
Do you want to improve at this company?

1333
01:10:02.300 --> 01:10:02.980
What do you want?

1334
01:10:03.140 --> 01:10:06.260
And Andy actually inspires someone.

1335
01:10:06.620 --> 01:10:06.940
Finally.

1336
01:10:06.940 --> 01:10:12.480
Well, listen, can I get out my bullshit card for a second?

1337
01:10:12.880 --> 01:10:15.080
Can I play my bullshit card?

1338
01:10:15.660 --> 01:10:15.860
Yeah.

1339
01:10:16.080 --> 01:10:17.340
I call bullshit on this.

1340
01:10:17.900 --> 01:10:22.040
Andy, I could give you the same speech you're giving Daryl.

1341
01:10:22.260 --> 01:10:26.420
You are no more qualified for this job than Daryl is.

1342
01:10:26.600 --> 01:10:27.780
You are a hot mess.

1343
01:10:27.780 --> 01:10:33.700
I mean, you are just the epitome of failing upwards, frankly.

1344
01:10:34.140 --> 01:10:41.460
And so I guess they're just two people who felt entitled to this job and one of them got it.

1345
01:10:41.600 --> 01:10:48.400
And the truth is that neither of them were maybe the best fit for the job.

1346
01:10:48.520 --> 01:10:54.520
But I call bullshit on Andy claiming that he was like the superior candidate.

1347
01:10:54.780 --> 01:10:56.040
I call bullshit.

1348
01:10:56.040 --> 01:10:57.700
I accept your bullshit card.

1349
01:10:57.860 --> 01:10:58.780
I think it is well played.

1350
01:10:59.060 --> 01:10:59.600
Thank you.

1351
01:11:00.400 --> 01:11:03.340
Next up, we have a ball tracker.

1352
01:11:05.980 --> 01:11:07.500
Please, what is it?

1353
01:11:07.800 --> 01:11:10.360
Daryl has a talking head where he says, you know what?

1354
01:11:10.500 --> 01:11:13.540
My future won't be determined by seven little white balls.

1355
01:11:13.760 --> 01:11:19.820
It will be determined by two big black balls because I control my destiny.

1356
01:11:20.220 --> 01:11:20.980
You're right.

1357
01:11:21.180 --> 01:11:21.680
Ball tracker.

1358
01:11:22.100 --> 01:11:23.020
Ball tracker.

1359
01:11:23.360 --> 01:11:25.300
Daryl and Andy are going to walk to the warehouse.

1360
01:11:25.300 --> 01:11:30.020
And they're going to see this greased pathway.

1361
01:11:30.840 --> 01:11:35.140
Erin is going to get loaded on some sort of a, what is it?

1362
01:11:35.220 --> 01:11:37.380
A slippery disc holding a box of paper.

1363
01:11:37.380 --> 01:11:38.860
And she has a helmet on.

1364
01:11:39.020 --> 01:11:41.520
And they're going to slingshot Erin.

1365
01:11:41.620 --> 01:11:42.420
Why Erin?

1366
01:11:42.560 --> 01:11:44.100
Why does Erin need to be on it?

1367
01:11:44.500 --> 01:11:48.020
Well, you know, when they were doing it just paper, it was flying everywhere.

1368
01:11:48.020 --> 01:11:53.660
So maybe they felt like they needed a driver, someone to steer the paper down the path.

1369
01:11:55.240 --> 01:11:58.160
Well, I texted Ellie about this.

1370
01:11:58.460 --> 01:12:02.340
I wanted to know, what was it like to slide on the grease?

1371
01:12:02.540 --> 01:12:03.220
Was it crazy?

1372
01:12:03.380 --> 01:12:04.100
Did you fall over?

1373
01:12:04.220 --> 01:12:04.700
How was it?

1374
01:12:04.840 --> 01:12:07.520
And she texted back, Jenna, is there something wrong with me?

1375
01:12:07.520 --> 01:12:09.520
I have no memory of doing that scene.

1376
01:12:09.960 --> 01:12:12.740
She said, I don't remember a thing about it.

1377
01:12:12.880 --> 01:12:15.200
She said, I don't even know basically what you're talking about.

1378
01:12:15.640 --> 01:12:16.480
Oh, my gosh.

1379
01:12:16.600 --> 01:12:18.360
She's completely blocked it out.

1380
01:12:18.600 --> 01:12:21.660
Well, I asked Steve Burgess and he said there's a good reason for that.

1381
01:12:21.800 --> 01:12:22.860
It's because it wasn't her.

1382
01:12:23.300 --> 01:12:25.720
It's a stunt person wearing that helmet.

1383
01:12:25.720 --> 01:12:27.560
Oh, any wonder she doesn't.

1384
01:12:27.640 --> 01:12:29.980
Yeah, it's a really good double for her.

1385
01:12:30.080 --> 01:12:31.840
So she never had to do it.

1386
01:12:32.280 --> 01:12:35.720
Please tell me you texted her back so she doesn't think she's losing it.

1387
01:12:35.940 --> 01:12:36.280
I did.

1388
01:12:36.360 --> 01:12:37.920
I texted her back and I told her that.

1389
01:12:38.020 --> 01:12:39.400
And she said, oh, thank goodness.

1390
01:12:39.400 --> 01:12:40.780
I was really concerned.

1391
01:12:41.460 --> 01:12:43.440
Yeah, you'd think you'd remember something like that.

1392
01:12:43.680 --> 01:12:44.060
Yeah.

1393
01:12:45.160 --> 01:12:50.200
This episode is going to end with a series of talking heads where everyone says what they

1394
01:12:50.200 --> 01:12:51.800
would do if they won the lottery.

1395
01:12:51.800 --> 01:12:56.900
My favorite was Toby's talking head because he said he would spend his free time making

1396
01:12:56.900 --> 01:13:00.740
his true crime podcast, The Flindersen Vials.

1397
01:13:02.200 --> 01:13:03.620
I would listen to that.

1398
01:13:03.780 --> 01:13:04.220
You would?

1399
01:13:04.640 --> 01:13:05.120
Yes.

1400
01:13:05.280 --> 01:13:06.000
To go to sleep.

1401
01:13:07.280 --> 01:13:08.820
That is so crazy.

1402
01:13:11.140 --> 01:13:13.920
Because I just imagined Toby's cadence.

1403
01:13:14.740 --> 01:13:16.300
Oh, that would put you to sleep.

1404
01:13:16.520 --> 01:13:17.120
You're right.

1405
01:13:17.480 --> 01:13:18.580
I get it now.

1406
01:13:18.700 --> 01:13:18.920
Yes.

1407
01:13:18.920 --> 01:13:25.420
The long pauses where he breaks down what happened.

1408
01:13:26.740 --> 01:13:27.300
Yeah.

1409
01:13:27.560 --> 01:13:29.800
The episode ends with a Pam and Jim talking head.

1410
01:13:30.000 --> 01:13:35.740
They have come to an agreement on their fantasy of what their life will be after they win the

1411
01:13:35.740 --> 01:13:36.040
lottery.

1412
01:13:36.040 --> 01:13:39.360
And I need to point out my hair in this talking head.

1413
01:13:39.720 --> 01:13:40.280
Oh.

1414
01:13:40.280 --> 01:13:42.200
I think I remember this.

1415
01:13:42.580 --> 01:13:49.480
If you look at it, it looks like I have those kind of curls, kind of like Nellie Olsen from

1416
01:13:49.480 --> 01:13:50.560
Little House on the Prairie.

1417
01:13:51.100 --> 01:13:53.080
They're like big barrel curls.

1418
01:13:53.200 --> 01:13:53.340
Yeah.

1419
01:13:53.960 --> 01:13:54.020
Yeah.

1420
01:13:54.180 --> 01:13:54.860
Around my head.

1421
01:13:55.320 --> 01:13:55.660
Yeah.

1422
01:13:55.760 --> 01:14:00.280
I am pretty sure what we would do in the mornings for my hair is we would curl it like

1423
01:14:00.280 --> 01:14:01.600
that, but then we would leave it.

1424
01:14:02.040 --> 01:14:03.260
To let it set.

1425
01:14:03.260 --> 01:14:03.800
Yes.

1426
01:14:04.040 --> 01:14:05.860
And we would go on and we would rehearse.

1427
01:14:06.040 --> 01:14:11.400
And then right before we got ready to shoot, then Kim Ferry, she would kind of like lightly

1428
01:14:11.400 --> 01:14:15.100
kind of brush out the curl with her fingertips or something.

1429
01:14:15.260 --> 01:14:17.060
It would be like her or Debbie would do it.

1430
01:14:17.480 --> 01:14:18.680
I think we forgot.

1431
01:14:19.180 --> 01:14:23.300
And we shot this talking head and we had not brushed out the curls.

1432
01:14:23.600 --> 01:14:25.940
And I have a memory of this happening once on the show.

1433
01:14:26.040 --> 01:14:27.000
And I think this was it.

1434
01:14:27.260 --> 01:14:29.200
And afterwards, we said something.

1435
01:14:29.200 --> 01:14:32.140
We said, oh my gosh, we forgot to brush out the curls.

1436
01:14:32.140 --> 01:14:33.060
And they were like, we don't care.

1437
01:14:33.240 --> 01:14:33.640
We got it.

1438
01:14:33.720 --> 01:14:34.200
It looks fine.

1439
01:14:34.360 --> 01:14:34.800
We don't care.

1440
01:14:35.200 --> 01:14:36.320
But now here it is.

1441
01:14:36.460 --> 01:14:38.500
All these years later, I'm watching this talking head.

1442
01:14:38.700 --> 01:14:39.800
And oh, yep, there it is.

1443
01:14:39.880 --> 01:14:41.340
That's the day we forgot.

1444
01:14:41.340 --> 01:14:42.640
We didn't brush out the curls.

1445
01:14:42.820 --> 01:14:42.980
Yeah.

1446
01:14:43.260 --> 01:14:43.700
Check it out.

1447
01:14:43.940 --> 01:14:47.600
Well, Jim and Pam, I guess their fantasies are finally meeting up, though.

1448
01:14:47.800 --> 01:14:51.460
They're going to have a like a New York type of brownstone, but it's going to be on

1449
01:14:51.460 --> 01:14:52.180
top of a mountain.

1450
01:14:53.080 --> 01:14:57.320
But yet it'll also be a short walk to like bookstores.

1451
01:14:57.320 --> 01:15:02.720
Well, it's a short subway stop at the top of the mountain from the best museuMs.

1452
01:15:03.180 --> 01:15:08.760
Jim can fish from Pam's pottery studio window, you know, but the schools are terrible.

1453
01:15:09.500 --> 01:15:10.540
Not good schools.

1454
01:15:10.540 --> 01:15:11.400
But what are you going to do?

1455
01:15:11.580 --> 01:15:12.440
What are you going to do?

1456
01:15:12.640 --> 01:15:13.140
Yeah.

1457
01:15:13.560 --> 01:15:20.200
Well, you know, maybe in their fantasy life, they've got to really force it to find common

1458
01:15:20.200 --> 01:15:20.560
ground.

1459
01:15:20.840 --> 01:15:21.960
Here you are again.

1460
01:15:22.180 --> 01:15:22.940
Here you are again.

1461
01:15:23.120 --> 01:15:23.980
Therapist Angela.

1462
01:15:25.720 --> 01:15:27.460
Well, guys, that was Lotto.

1463
01:15:27.840 --> 01:15:33.160
A big thank you to Steve Burgess for all of his awesome behind the scenes info and also

1464
01:15:33.160 --> 01:15:35.180
to Charlie Grandy and Ellie Kemper.

1465
01:15:35.420 --> 01:15:39.740
And to Mark for helping us kick off this episode and talking to us about playing Nate.

1466
01:15:40.060 --> 01:15:41.060
How much fun.

1467
01:15:41.420 --> 01:15:43.160
We had such a great time today.

1468
01:15:43.320 --> 01:15:46.660
We hope you enjoyed listening and we will see you next week.

1469
01:15:46.800 --> 01:15:47.380
See you then.

1470
01:15:47.720 --> 01:15:54.270
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.

